Convex 1.41.0 and Workpool 0.4.8. An idempotent sync action always throws after its HTTP request receives a 503 response. One mounted pool is configured as follows. One action is enqueued with an onComplete callback and no per-enqueue retry option.

```ts
const pool = new Workpool(components.workpool, {
  maxParallelism: 3,
  defaultRetryBehavior: { maxAttempts: 3, initialBackoffMs: 100, base: 2 },
});
```

Convex 1.41.0 and @convex-dev/workpool 0.4.8. Image jobs and export jobs each make one awaited request to the same service. The service permits at most five requests at once across both workloads. No other code calls it. The app currently uses two separately mounted pools:

```ts
// convex/convex.config.ts
import { defineApp } from "convex/server";
import workpool from "@convex-dev/workpool/convex.config";
const app = defineApp();
app.use(workpool, { name: "images" });
app.use(workpool, { name: "exports" });
export default app;
```

```ts
// convex/images.ts
import { Workpool } from "@convex-dev/workpool";
import { components } from "./_generated/api";
export const imagePool = new Workpool(components.images, { maxParallelism: 5 });
```

```ts
// convex/exports.ts
import { Workpool } from "@convex-dev/workpool";
import { components } from "./_generated/api";
export const exportPool = new Workpool(components.exports, { maxParallelism: 5 });
```
